#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:7
#: 23129642dec6452a932518f45e70aa3b
msgid "Loading Firmware via SD Card"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:9
#: feff6b904d1141c4a418a84e983a4a11
msgid "It is possible to update the ArduPilot firmware on certain autopilots by placing a specifically-named file onto an SD card and running the autopilot's bootloader (e.g. by power-cycling the board)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:11
#: e428a67a00084196988a15010e8a8c9a
msgid "at this time only a few autopilots have this capability. See instructions below to determine if an autopilot has this feature. Only H7 based autopilots using MMC connected SD cards are capable of this and not all that do have had the feature added as of yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:14
#: db55edd7b49641478472f3fb31b71270
msgid "Why would I want to do this?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:15
#: 9da4d5a6365e4b889b495760c0b4ade1
msgid "There are several reasons this technique may be of use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:17
#: 56276d525f0641329561d4b3ccb7d97c
msgid "There is no convenient, reliable access to the vehicle's USB port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:18
#: 109cc2ea151b4ed89d5ea7ca0283b938
msgid "It is desired to update the vehicle firmware over a telemetry radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:19
#: d6efa074a0374deab99c380f263caf80
msgid "The vehicle is remote and the local operators may struggle with the normal interfaces to update the firmware. This allows OEMs to remotely add an updated file onto users' SD cards which would upload on the next boot of the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:22
#: 614684faa6574898a510b3d5945f88b8
msgid "Is my autopilot capable of this?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:23
#: 4fef612aea5143d0835448e18b9a7c2a
msgid "In order to do this several elements must be present:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:25
#: e0fd736e785447429d86c8f409a9343b
msgid "The autopilot must have SD card capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:26
#: 127e5837384f4393ab6e2f68b09c51de
msgid "The SD card must be enabled in its bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:27
#: 98b291ab9f0349b49d25d46debde1e64
msgid "The bootloader code and flashing firmware must be enabled in the autopilots firmware definition files (hwdefs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:29
#: 28cc6e364dd7481095408d051d0bf23d
msgid "To see if a given autopilot has this capability, you can check in its firmware folder on the `Firmware build server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ to see if it has a ``xxxxxx.abin`` file present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:32
#: 5eb4b79702414c809017fc233f3ad943
msgid "The Bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:33
#: aac7bdf907cf4dae9b94ba59012dc05f
msgid "A bootloader capable of flashing from the SD card is required (and the autopilot must have SD card capability, obviously). Newer autopilot's with SD cards may or may not have this capability and a capable bootloader included in their hardware definition (if not, see :ref:`Building capable firmware yourself <building-autoflash-firmware>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:35
#: 6266f2368a2b4e958e404420614eedd0
msgid "If the autopilot firmware currently provides this capability, updating your current bootloader may be required to support flashing from SD card.  Note that updating the autopilot's bootloader is an operation which can make your board non-operational, and difficult to recover.  More-so with boards that do not expose a \"boot0\" pin, such as the CubeOrange.  Be aware of this risk, and be prepared to spend considerable time recovering a board if something bad happens when updating the bootloader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:37
#: a8677c4dd3dd4bcc89046bcc4a615993
msgid ":ref:`The instructions on updating the bootloader <common-bootloader-update>` can be followed to update your bootloader; be aware that you must use a recent firmware (4.5 or higher) to obtain a suitable bootloader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:40
#: e7954776e0d94e08b7e8ae893b9f64ff
msgid "The Firmware File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:41
#: 4d585f3656694deaba24473902904749
msgid "The file to be loaded onto the SD card is of a specially named \"xxxxx.abin\" file created for this purpose.  This is a binary file with a small amount of text providing some information about the binary. Most notably, a checksum which the bootloader will verify before attempting to flash the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:43
#: 830a0d40573d4eacab1936c8fbda203e
msgid "Boards which support flash-from-sdcard will also have ``.abin`` files available for download from the `Firmware build server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:46
#: 059e5a5b06ba44769e4e5ca965d03f3c
msgid "Firmware File Name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:47
#: 4aaaae3270fa4bd19a42023c544f457d
msgid "The filename which is used when generating firmware is ***not*** the correct name to use when placing the firmware on the SD card.  When the ``.abin`` files are generated they contain the vehicle name, for example, \"arduplane.abin\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:49
#: 91ad6378a20545bca8d29c9261722720
msgid "There is only one correct filename that may be used to flash-from-sdcard; this is ``ardupilot.abin``.  When placing the file on the SD card, ensure the file has been renamed to ``ardupilot.abin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:52
#: e37c9351016c4c5aaa4d6d4eb219d220
msgid "Transferring the File to the SD card"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:53
#: 9d74c88147e94bfaa6f992bf69754b70
msgid "This can be done in your operating system as you would ordinarily interact with the SD card (e.g. file browser)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:55
#: 6a68776b6bd94fc889f110e8fff7bf5f
msgid "You can also transfer the file to the SD card's base directory via ``MAVFTP`` using Mission Planner or similar GCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:60
#: edef384151984881b960771992689385
msgid "Ensure the file is the correct size before continuing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:62
#: a9880958dfef448a83298533e457f611
msgid "After the transfer is complete, the directory listing should look something like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:76
#: 6e2a6d2ff848417395768b8cd409640e
msgid "Triggering the Flash Update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:77
#: e7cf03d572a047dd921f16583dc189d9
msgid "Power cycle the board to enter the bootloader which will automatically check for the firmware update file and begin flashing it.  Alternatively to avoid the powercycle the autopilot may be rebooted via a `PREFLIGHT_REBOOT_SHUTDOWN <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#MAV_CMD_PREFLIGHT_REBOOT_SHUTDOWN>`__ command with the 'Param1' field set to 3 (ie. \"Reboot autopilot and keep it in the bootloader until upgraded\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:79
#: b6762bdc38fd49199a8f2eac939ae3e5
msgid "It should take roughly 1 minute to verify the firmware and flash it to the vehicle's internal flash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:81
#: 83240594363a4396811ffb4ebc5f8e8e
msgid "If the process completes successfully the file will renamed to ``ardupilot-flashed.abin``.  The vehicle should proceed to boot the firmware once flashing is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:84
#: e7f135d5b32c46eea6f86b2ca08c62a8
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:85
#: b5df5c28cd09432699644f4ec9d7c295
msgid "Several things can go wrong with the firmware flash, but some diagnostics are available to help work out what the problem might be."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:87
#: a35c615ca9ff4b5d9ca266da54a3f563
msgid "At each stage of the flashing process, the ``ardupilot.abin`` file is renamed to reflect the stage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:88
#: 9970972ae9524b48a64e34795f51ccc5
msgid "if the file is called ``ardupilot-verify.abin`` then the process failed when trying to checksum the file, or the board was interrupted when doing so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:89
#: 87f55355c7cb45f39c60da09bdb9d96d
msgid "if the file is called ``ardupilot-verify-failed.abin`` then the checksum the bootloader calculated did not match the bootloader in the ``.abin`` metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:90
#: 97e363d4ff1d4c97894877ca767436c2
msgid "if the file is called ``ardupilot-flash.abin`` the process failed when writing the firmware, or the board was interrupted while doing so.  The board is unlikely to boot into an ArduPilot firmware if this has happened, so a re-flash will be required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:91
#: 2df9730dac9d406ea3cebe9ac0d2c8ef
msgid "if the file is called ``ardupilot-flashed.abin`` you should not need this \"troubleshooting\" section, as the flash process has succeeded!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:96
#: 64bc78a7afea4107ad778bb30cb562e1
msgid "Building the firmware yourself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-install-sdcard.rst:98
#: 0d6a023ea093432ebb554c8818054be9
msgid "If the autopilot has an SD card capability but no SD Card flash-able firmware is present on the `Firmware build server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__, you can build the firmware yourself. You must setup a build environment and then modify the autopilot's hwdefs to build a capable bootloader and an ``xxxx.abin`` firmware, see :ref:`building-the-code`."
msgstr ""

